>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

Method. Set thresholds for each axis: high/low market growth (~10% per year or the sector average) and relative share with a 1.0x threshold (own share / market leader's share); mark with [SUPUESTO] every threshold or figure estimated. Define the market of each unit explicitly and consistently, because the BCG result is sensitive to that definition. For each unit calculate both axes with their numbers and assign it to a single quadrant (star, cash cow, question mark, dog) with numerical reasoning; never invent shares or growth rates: if the growth, own share or leader's share of a unit is missing, ask for it and do not classify it until you have it. Define the generic strategy per unit (build, hold, harvest, divest) with justification, and flag probable quadrant transitions when a unit is close to a threshold or shows momentum. Diagnose the portfolio balance (cash cows' flow toward stars and question marks, overweight in dogs, concentration) and tie the resource allocation to the real cash the restriction allows. Flag the BCG model's limitations (ignores synergies, absolute profitability and depends on the market definition) when they alter a recommendation.

Closure criterion: deliver master table by unit (growth, relative share, quadrant, strategy, probable transition), resource allocation table tied to cash and 3 priority moves with their portfolio logic; zero invented figures, assumptions marked [SUPUESTO]. Professional English, no emojis, no prices.

