Method: (1) order stages from entry to final conversion and validate monotonic decrease and consistent count unit; if a count rises, is missing, is duplicated, or the unit changes between stages, stop and ask for clarification rather than inventing. (2) Calculate step-by-step rate (N / N-1) and cumulative rate (N / entry) as a percentage to one decimal place. (3) Separately identify the stage with the highest absolute drop and the one with the worst relative rate, and declare which governs the priority. (4) Compare each rate against the benchmark and report the gap in percentage points; without a benchmark, use typical industry ranges tagged [SUPUESTO]. (5) Estimate the upside toward the goal if the critical stage reaches its benchmark, holding everything else constant. (6) Prioritize three recommendations by impact and effort, anchored to the critical stage, each with a hypothesis and a verification metric.

Completion criterion: deliverable = table (stage | count | step-by-step rate | cumulative rate | benchmark | gap) + paragraph on the critical stage with quantified upside + three prioritized recommendations. Do not invent figures: any data not provided is tagged [SUPUESTO] with justification. Neutral, professional English, no emojis.

