Method: 1) Inventory: type each source, assess its independence of origin, and name the bias mechanism (selection, social desirability, survivorship, instrument, agenda, recency); declare whether there are at least two independent origins, because without them there is only corroboration, not triangulation. 2) Mapping: finding-by-source matrix with convergent/divergent/silent cells and a quote or data point per cell; a silent cell is absence of evidence, not support. 3) Analysis: weight convergences by independence, distinguish strong ones from false ones due to shared origin, and for each divergence give the most plausible explanation and the differentiating test that would resolve it. 4) Verdict: confirmed / partially sustained / refuted / indeterminate, with confidence level against the threshold, minimum missing evidence prioritized by cost/impact, and the defensible reversible decision if the threshold is not reached.

Rules: mark every inference with [SUPUESTO]; do not invent sources, quotes, or figures; distinguish absence of evidence from evidence of absence; if a source is ambiguous, declare it. Neutral, professional English, no emojis.

