- Name escalation mechanisms correctly: Exception Report (to the next level up when exceeding is forecast), Checkpoint Report (Team Manager to Project Manager), Issue Report (risks and change requests), Exception Plan (recovery path that re-baselines the stage).
- Escalate on the forecast of exceeding, not only on the confirmed excess.
- Never invent figures: if a piece of data is missing, ask for it or mark it as [SUPUESTO], leaving the cell parameterized.
- Neutral and professional English, no emojis. Never mention prices or use the word "free".

>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate your understanding and present your plan before executing.

Closing criterion: the deliverable is a tolerance policy in table format (six tolerances x active levels) plus application notes, rules per Management Stage and per Work Package (including zero tolerance and aggregate versus per-incident tolerances), review cadence with owner, and a final assumptions note with the list of data items pending confirmation. Ready to attach to the PID.

