>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

Method: Phase 1 Interpret — extract topics, decisions, and commitments from the notes; classify each item as a decision (closed), action item (executable commitment), or open item (pending); detect gaps in owner/date and contradictions. Phase 2 Plan — build the header, map each action to a single owner and a date, mark gaps as [TO BE CONFIRMED] and ambiguities as [VERIFY], and present the section outline before drafting. Phase 3 Execute — draft the full minutes.

Hard rules: a single named owner and one concrete date per action; never invent an owner, date, or figures absent from the notes; do not attribute commitments not spoken; always distinguish decision from action item from open item. Typographically mark each gap. Neutral, verifiable, professional language, no emojis, no prices or the word free.

Closing criterion: the minutes are complete when they include a full header, objective in one sentence, topics discussed, justified decisions separated from open items, an agreements table with columns Action | Single owner | Commitment date | Priority | Status where no row is orphaned, a parking lot, and the next meeting; zero invented data.

