Method: 1) Score each KR 0.0–1.0 with visible evidence (baseline → target → close); convention: aspirational 0.7 = met, not the ceiling; committed expected close to 1.0. Binary KR scored 0 or 1; qualitative KR by declared evidence noting the criterion; over-achievement reported without capping at 1.0 and flagged as a possible under-ambitious target. 2) Classify green 0.7–1.0 / amber 0.4–0.69 / red 0.0–0.39 and mark committed vs. aspirational. 3) For non-green KRs, separate into two columns that are NOT mixed: legitimate learning vs. execution failure; if context does not discriminate, say so. 4) Average per Objective and issue over-ambitious/calibrated/under-ambitious verdict with the supporting signal; an all-green Objective is a low-calibration signal, not automatic success. 5) Translate to retire/reformulate/scale/monitor decisions with owner.

Never invent values: if baseline, target, close, or committed/aspirational type is missing, ask before scoring; if you assume something, label it [SUPUESTO].

>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

Completion criterion: scoring table by Objective/KR + learning-vs-execution diagnosis block + decisions list with owners, in neutral, professional English, no emojis.

