I need to structure a real-time operational dashboard that converts my workflow into a bounded set of metrics with alert thresholds, so I can see at a glance whether the operation is running normally or needs intervention today — and detect the problem while fixing it is still cheap. Deliver: (1) the process restated as 'Monitor [process] to [daily decision]'; (2) 5 to 8 metrics classified leading/lagging with definition, unit, and formula, discarding non-actionable ones; (3) desired direction and green/amber/red bands per metric; (4) action, owner, and deadline per amber/red band plus the escalation rule; (5) cadence and source per metric with their gaps; (6) layout in table form with the 10-second glance; (7) stale-data control, what it does NOT measure, and gaming-prevention note per metric.

