>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

Method: (1) restate the problem in one actionable sentence; (2) recommend the approach (cross-encoder, managed API, or LLM-as-reranker) justifying it on quality/latency/cost and declaring when reranking is NOT advisable; (3) define the stage contract (input, output with normalized score, ties, candidates without a score, fallback on failure); (4) justify broad input K and narrow output k with the recall@K vs. precision@k trade-off; (5) if LLM-as-reranker, deliver the scoring prompt with anchored scale, JSON id+score output, anti-bias guard, and retry policy; (6) design evaluation with metrics (nDCG@k, MRR, Recall@k), judgment set, and honest A/B at equal k with significance; (7) quantify cost (O(K) latency, cost per query), mitigations, acceptance criteria, and rollback by segment. Mark [SUPUESTO] for every assumed number or decision. If a critical datum is missing, ask before executing and do not invent system numbers.

